  <h2>Highway Design Standards</h2>

  <p>SR-177 is engineered to meet the demands of a <strong>65 mph limited-access highway</strong> incorporating "Dark Sky" compliant lighting and noise-reducing pavement.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %} The Weber County extension is being planned to the same design standards as the completed Davis County segment, with the 250-foot ROW footprint accommodating four travel lanes, a median, and multi-use trail corridors on both sides.{% cite "udot-ses-build" %}</p>

